<p>Amaretto (Italian for <em>‘a little bitter’</em>) is a sweet Liqueur that originated in Saronno (a commune in Lombardy, Italy).</p>
<p>Depending on the brand, Amaretto can be made from a variety of ingredients including apricot kernels, peach stones, bitter almonds, or just regular almonds. The key is that all of these ingredients contain <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benzaldehyde" rel="noopener">benzaldehyde</a> which acts as the almond-like flavour of the liqueur.</p>
<p>Amaretto usually contains between 21 to 28 per cent alcohol by volume.</p>
